WEBVTT

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.870
What's the truth that lies behind the human soul?

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.980
The five of spades.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.910
Not again.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:21.910
I quit.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.870
This is stupid.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.000
Excuse me...

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.800
are you by any chance Saitou Yakumo-san?

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.880
Yes, I am. Do you see anyone else here?

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.010
One of the seniors in my club told me about you.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.680
They said that you've got psychic powers,

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.270
and that you're really knowledgeable about ghosts and the like-

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.770
Who are you?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.770
Oh, I'm Ozawa Haruka.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:54.900
I'm a member of the Faculty of Arts, the Department of Education-

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.150
Just your name's fine.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.780
I... see...

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.120
So? What do you want?

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.740
Um, can you keep what I'm about to tell you a secret?

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.330
Why?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.080
It's about something that happened in the old building which is off limits.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.300
It was about two weeks ago...

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.220
That night we were holding a farewell party for one of the seniors.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.470
Someone proposed a test of courage and we all decided to participate.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.060
So, the six of us all entered the old building.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.770
So, this is the forbidden room?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.530
This place is kinda boring, isn't it?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.740
Did you guys hear something?

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.240
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.080
Let's quickly take a photo and get out of here.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.580
Let's take one with our backs against the piano.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.800
Wh-What's that?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.050
What the hell?!

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.560
And then, ten days after that...

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.360
You there, what's wrong?

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.530
Miki's still in the hospital...

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:31.290
Next was Kazuhiko-kun. He became possessed soon after that,

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.250
and jumped off a building.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.290
That story you just told...

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:42.800
Did you actually witness your friend's death yourself?

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.930
No.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.180
Someone told me about it.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:51.930
In that case, we can't be certain that a ghost actually possessed him.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:56.940
But he's not the type of person who'd commit suicide. That's why he-

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.650
Just stick to the plain facts. Keep your personal feelings out of it.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.030
Otherwise, I won't be able to figure out what really happened.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:05.530
I'm sorry.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.030
So, what do you want from me?

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.200
I want you to save Miki.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.500
I don't care whether you use exorcism or purification; as long as it works, anything's fine.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.330
Huh?

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.880
25,000 yen, including tax.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.970
I'll take 10,000 yen right now as a deposit.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.880
You won't do this for free?

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.760
Are we friends?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.590
No.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.890
Are we lovers?

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.850
I-In your dreams!

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.230
Then, don't you think it's odd for me to help you

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.600
with no strings attached, when we're neither friends nor lovers?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:40.770
W-Well, that's true, but...

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.490
A mirror?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:53.700
That card guessing game you played earlier... You were cheating, weren't you?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.710
You're the first person to have noticed that trick.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.710
I'm leaving.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.600
Fine.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.510
Let's go.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.270
Take me to the hospital where Miki is.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.270
So, I'm your next victim, eh?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.610
It's entirely up to you whether you trust me or not.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.360
However,

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.320
I <i>can</i> see ghosts.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.870
I can even communicate with them.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.740
You're just talking a load of nonsense now.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.210
You're right in thinking that I don't have the power nor knowledge to perform an exorcism or a purification ritual.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.750
In fact, I can only see them.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:47.510
But if I can talk some sense into the ghost, I may be able to save her.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.680
Please excuse me for disturbing you.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.430
You had a sister, didn't you?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.810
Her name was Ayaka, wasn't it?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:02.150
You were both the same age. In fact, she was your twin.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.110
She died in a car accident, didn't she?

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.860
She died because...

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.740
Please stop.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:19.120
I don't care what happens to your friend.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.630
It's entirely your decision whether you want to trust me or not.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:31.630
As you can see, she's extremely weak.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.390
The doctors said that if she continues on like this, she'll die.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.600
They haven't been able to come up with a diagnosis either...

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.140
Figures.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.690
Miki!

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.450
I see, so that's what happened to you...

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.280
What did he look like?

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.720
Will Miki be all right?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:20.350
You were right. Souls of the dead are possessing her.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.890
They're all murdered women.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.650
Murdered?!

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:32.110
Normally, they either remain where they're killed or where their corpses are dumped.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:33.950
That means...

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:40.120
They were either killed in that room or their corpses were dumped there.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:49.710
I-Is it true that Yuichi-kun's dead?!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.050
Yeah... he committed suicide.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:56.470
Though... I'm not sure something like that can be described as suicide...

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.310
It was exactly like what happened to Miki-kun the other day.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.480
I was talking to him on the station platform when he suddenly started behaving strangely,

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.690
and jumped straight onto the tracks.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.060
That can't be...

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.780
That's right. I heard the four of you sneaked into the old building.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.490
How did you know?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.120
Yuichi-kun told me.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.330
There have been a lot of eerie rumors about that building for many years now.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.710
I bet that this is the work of the ghosts' curse.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:28.920
The question now is whether the police will believe me or not.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.710
Let's keep the existence of ghosts a secret between the two of us for now.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:34.670
All right?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.130
Okay...

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.770
Well, good night.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:57.700
Um, you're heading back to the university, right?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.990
In which case, you're going the wrong way.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.370
I'm walking you home.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:02.990
What?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.250
Um...

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.460
No, it's fine. I can get home by myself.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.630
You're really stupid, aren't you?

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.340
I see...

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.920
You're in danger too.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.470
But you said yourself that you can't do anything except see ghosts.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:24.220
The one who's after you is human.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.230
Human?

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.350
Either way, you should avoid being alone,

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.730
and remain by my side as much as possible.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:39.110
Does that mean that you'll protect me?

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.990
You ask too many questions.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:53.210
Hello, I'm Saitou. I'm a member of the Supernatural Phenomena Research Club.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:59.470
Even if you give me this, I still can't let you inside.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:04.850
If you really must enter, you'll have to get Takaoka-san's permission first.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.560
The professor's?

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:17.320
I never realized he was in charge of the old building.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.320
That bothered me on our way here too, but...

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.080
Ah! Um...

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:34.130
Saitou-san... what's wrong?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.460
Take a look at this.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.310
He's the one who murdered those women and your friends,

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.810
then made it look like your friends committed suicide.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:56.860
Takaoka-sensei? You're joking, right?

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:01.320
When I checked the blueprints in the library, I found that there's a basement underneath that room.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:07.370
He either killed those women there or he's hiding their corpses there.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.660
Why do you suspect him?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:15.290
Why didn't they enter the forbidden room?

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.800
That's because we decided that they'd prefer to be alone together...

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:26.050
Do you remember what Takaoka said to you when he was warning you?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.890
I heard the four of you sneaked into the old building.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:35.150
A total of six people entered the old building.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.940
However, only four of you entered the forbidden room.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:43.280
There's no way he could know this unless he was present in that room.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.280
That means...

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:52.960
He was in the basement the night you all entered the room.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:56.040
That's why he assumed that only four people had entered the old building.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:06.430
But isn't it also possible that Yuichi-kun gave him the wrong number in the first place?

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:11.390
Personally, I'm skeptical of everything he's said so far.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.190
However, your theory is also entirely plausible,

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.730
which is why we need evidence.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.490
This is evidence.

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:36.710
Blasted cat. He calls me up yet he's late himself.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.670
Smoking is prohibited on campus, Goto-san.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.880
Yakumo, I haven't lit up yet.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.600
Ah, so you've finally grown up, eh?

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.680
It's not what you're thinking.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.810
Don't be so modest.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.440
If you don't keep a tight leash on her, she'll run away.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.440
What? Like your wife?

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.690
That's none of your business.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.570
Who was that?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.830
He may not look it, but he's a policeman.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.200
You're acquainted with a policeman?

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.580
It's more like a fated bond.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.210
He really does remind me of a cat.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.130
Did you say something?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.510
Nope, it's nothing.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.850
More importantly, how much longer do you plan on being my bodyguard?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:35.140
The police will intervene when the forensic report is in.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.770
You just need to bear with it until then.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:38.810
Fine.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:43.110
Don't get the wrong idea. I'm the one who's putting up with things.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.030
So? Did you check it out?

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.990
Now, just calm down.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:59.540
How does sipping tea while viewing my spleen collection sound?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.040
Never, you disgusting geezer.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.680
Don't go off on your own.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:14.050
But... I need to...

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.560
Come straight back.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:34.320
The fingerprints found on these items and the ones on the paper cup were identical.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:40.160
In addition, a further set of fingerprints, believed to be that of the owners, were found on each of these items.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.920
When I looked into it further, I discovered that the fingerprints belong to people reported missing.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.210
It's just as that blasted cat suspected.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.700
It would look far too suspicious if all of you committed suicide.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.990
I'll just have to make you disappear.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:25.080
It's your own fault. You violated this holy room.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.920
There's no need to be scared.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:34.220
There are a lot of friends waiting for you... all those rotting corpses that sleep in the basement.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.440
Takaoka-sensei is-

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.370
Saitou-san!

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:02.660
You don't have to worry about me.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.170
Wh-What's wrong with your eye?!

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.340
My red left eye allows me to see the ghosts of those

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:22.060
who remain attached to this world even after their deaths.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:31.150
The ghosts of all those left in the basement are still suffering.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:32.440
G-Get away from me!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:38.320
Do you understand... their regret?

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.330
Saitou-san...

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:45.500
You're the one who should atone for your sins!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.180
You must be Takaoka.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:07.980
I'm with the police.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:09.810
You'll be coming with me now.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.320
This way's no good either.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.200
We've got no choice but to head for the roof.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.870
But the stairs are on fire too.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.330
Don't worry. I've memorized the layout of this building.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.040
Just hurry up!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.210
It's just behind Meisei University.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.460
Yakumo!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.340
I've arrested Takaoka and I've called the fire brigade.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.260
Hang on tight!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:37.970
Get back!

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:38.720
Yakumo!

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:50.650
If we inform the ghosts that have possessed Miki that Takaoka's been arrested,

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:52.860
they should leave her body.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.400
Miki will be saved, right?

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:59.030
But Kazuhiko-kun and Yuichi-kun...

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.820
they won't be coming back...

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:05.330
I still have one question remaining.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:10.250
Why did you enter the old building?

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:14.840
You don't seem like a risk-taker.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:22.930
Did you perhaps think that the ghost of your deceased sister was there?

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.930
I... heard rumors.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.730
People said that they heard <i>Etude
Op. 10, No. 3</i>  by Chopin

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.560
playing from the old building even though it was supposed to be empty.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:41.450
My sister used to study the piano. That was her best piece.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:51.370
She was really cute and good-natured. Everyone loved her.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:20:04.090
That day, I figured I'd be a little mean to her.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:19.940
I never imagined that it would turn out that way...

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:22.570
She probably still hates me for it.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:24.780
You're wrong.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.870
She was the one who told me you were in danger.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.870
Your sister doesn't bear you any grudges.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.390
I... want to see her.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.980
It's beautiful...

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.030
Close your eyes...

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.590
Sister?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:32.970
You'll be fine without me now, right?

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:35.060
Yes.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:42.150
Goodbye, sister.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.330
Thank you.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:18.810
You saw it, right? The poor ghost that's stuck at the bottom of this river.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:24.610
However, if you obey me, your daughter will be revived.

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:26.490
Please.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.110
Please save my daughter.

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:39.370
The truth behind human souls is...

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:43.750
darkness.
